BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:uj-artists-in-residence-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261030T081527Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260831
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260901
SUMMARY:Deadline: University of Johannesburg Artists in Residence 2027
DESCRIPTION:UJ Arts & Culture's annual residency gives artists a monthly st
 ipend and an institutional base at the University of Johannesburg for ten 
 months\, with the option of a remote rather than physical residency. Disci
 plines covered are visual and fine arts\, music\, theatre\, performance an
 d dance\, design\, film and television\, and literary arts. A virtual info
 rmation session with Pieter Jacobs\, Head of UJ Arts & Culture\, was sched
 uled for 17 August 2026 to walk applicants through the process. ELIGIBILIT
 Y: applicants must hold a relevant post-school qualification\, with prefer
 ence for master's and PhD holders\, and must not be affiliated with anothe
 r tertiary institution in South Africa. Preference has historically gone t
 o artists with African connections. APPLICATION: via the online form linke
 d from the UJ Arts & Culture residency page\; contact kmachoga@uj.ac.za or
  +27 11 559 1476 with questions. DEADLINE: 31 August 2026. No fee.\n\nOrga
 nisation: UJ Arts & Culture\, University of Johannesburg\nLocation: Johann
 esburg\, South Africa. Both physical and remote residencies can be applied
  for\, though office\, studio\, rehearsal and performance space is limited
  and not guaranteed.\nAward: Stipend of ZAR 12\,000 per month across a 10-
 month residency\, so roughly ZAR 120\,000 in total. No travel or accommoda
 tion budget on top of the stipend\, and studio or rehearsal space is limit
 ed rather than guaranteed. No application fee.\nDuration: 10 months during
  2027\n\nMore: https://arts.uj.ac.za/artists-in-residence/?utm_source=arti
 ficialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://arts.uj.ac.za/artists-in-residence/?utm_source=artificialnouvea
 ugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Johannesburg\, South Africa. Both physical and remote residencies 
 can be applied for\, though office\, studio\, rehearsal and performance sp
 ace is limited and not guaranteed.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:delfina-gulbenkian-artists-portugal-lusophone-africa-2027@artificialnou
 veau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261030T081527Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261004
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261005
SUMMARY:Deadline: Delfina Foundation x Calouste Gulbenkian Foundation: Open
  Call for Artists from Portugal and Portuguese-Speaking African Nations (L
 ondon residency)
DESCRIPTION:In partnership with the Calouste Gulbenkian Foundation (UK Bran
 ch)\, Delfina Foundation welcomes applications from contemporary visual ar
 tists from Portugal\, Angola\, Mozambique\, Guinea-Bissau\, Cape Verde and
  Sao Tome and Principe for a London residency from 28 June to 17 September
  2027\, during Delfina's open summer season dedicated to independent resea
 rch. ELIGIBILITY: applicants must be born in one of the six eligible count
 ries (individuals currently based in the UK are not eligible)\; be seeking
  to develop their practice through research\; be able to explain how an in
 ternational residency may benefit their career development and local netwo
 rks\; and be proficient in English (the interview is conducted in English)
 . Collectives and duos are advised to put forth one member to be in reside
 nce. THE PROGRAMME: alongside time and space to develop their work\, resid
 ents get guided visits to museums\, galleries\, non-profits\, artist-run s
 paces and studios\, plus trips to institutions outside London\; opportunit
 ies to meet artists\, curators\, academics and researchers through organis
 ed presentations\, studio visits\, events and meals\; professional develop
 ment including presentations and crits\, portfolio reviews and mentoring\;
  and collaborative exchange between residents through informal gatherings 
 and meals. APPLY via the online application form (Cognito Forms\, save-and
 -resume supported)\; Delfina strongly recommends reading the Guidance Note
 s document carefully before starting. All applicants notified by mid-Novem
 ber 2026. Deadline Sunday 4 October 2026\, 23:59 BST.\n\nOrganisation: Del
 fina Foundation\, in partnership with the Calouste Gulbenkian Foundation (
 UK Branch)\nLocation: Delfina Foundation\, 29-31 Catherine Place\, London\
 , UK. Applicants must be born in Portugal\, Angola\, Mozambique\, Guinea-B
 issau\, Cape Verde or Sao Tome and Principe\; individuals currently based 
 in the UK are not eligible.\nAward: Twelve-week fully funded residency: a 
 return economy-class flight\, airport transfers in the UK\, reimbursement 
 of visa fees if required\, a living allowance of GBP 40 per day\, a materi
 als budget of GBP 1\,200\, a travel pass for London's public transport net
 work\, and a single bedroom with a desk at Delfina Foundation\, a house ho
 sting up to eight residents with shared bathrooms\, laundry rooms\, kitche
 n\, library and dining room. No application fee.\nDuration: Twelve weeks\,
  28 June to 17 September 2027\, during Delfina's open summer 2027 residenc
 y season.\n\nMore: https://www.delfinafoundation.com/open-calls/current/op
 en-call-for-artists-from-portugal-or-portugese-speaking-african-nations/?u
 tm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.delfinafoundation.com/open-calls/current/open-call-for-arti
 sts-from-portugal-or-portugese-speaking-african-nations/?utm_source=artifi
 cialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Delfina Foundation\, 29-31 Catherine Place\, London\, UK. Applican
 ts must be born in Portugal\, Angola\, Mozambique\, Guinea-Bissau\, Cape V
 erde or Sao Tome and Principe\; individuals currently based in the UK are 
 not eligible.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stimuleringsfonds-think-tanger-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.
 io
DTSTAMP:20261030T081527Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261021
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261022
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stimuleringsfonds: Open Call Residency Think Tanger 2027 
 (Tangier\, Morocco)
DESCRIPTION:The Creative Industries Fund NL (Stimuleringsfonds) is recruiti
 ng one Netherlands-based designer\, architect\, spatial practitioner or ma
 ker for a two-month residency in 2027 at Think Tanger\, a multidisciplinar
 y cultural platform dedicated to stimulating culture\, creativity\, innova
 tion and exchange in Tangier\, Morocco. Founded in 2016\, Think Tanger uni
 tes artists\, designers\, researchers\, entrepreneurs and local communitie
 s to explore the urban and cultural dynamics of a city in transformation a
 nd to promote understanding and dialogue\, working through alternative edu
 cation\, creative entrepreneurship\, art production and participatory rese
 arch. The residency was set up with the Fund to stimulate crossovers and e
 xperiments\, initiate exchanges and learn from other people's perspectives
 \, knowledge and ideas. It offers the opportunity to carry out research\, 
 expand your network and develop new work with a focus on design\, urbanism
  and socio-spatial dynamics\, creatively researching existing presuppositi
 ons and social issues in Tangier's unique urban context. ELIGIBILITY: you 
 are an individual designer\, architect\, spatial practitioner or maker\; y
 ou are established in the Netherlands\, Aruba\, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Saba\,
  Sint Eustatius or Sint Maarten (Kingdom of the Netherlands)\; you are reg
 istered in the business register of the Dutch Chamber of Commerce (KvK) or
  another business register within the Kingdom of the Netherlands\; and you
  have had a professional practice in the creative industry for at least tw
 o years (note: a lower bar than the four years required by the Fund's othe
 r 2027 residencies). NOT open to duos\, collectives or cooperative venture
 s\, nor to designers and makers who receive a grant during the work period
  under the Talent Development Grant Scheme\, the Open Call Self-taught Des
 igner or the Open Call Emerging Design Practices ABCSSS\; accepting this o
 pen call means you cannot apply to those schemes and open calls in 2027. F
 UNDING: EUR 5\,500 subsidy for the two-month residency. Assessment takes t
 he form of a tender: an external advisory committee ranks proposals on the
  artistic quality of the work\, the quality of the proposed project and th
 e motivation in relation to the goals of the residency\, and the highest-s
 coring proposal is awarded. Decision within eight weeks of the closing dat
 e. Submit via the Creative Industries Fund NL by 21 October 2026\, 16:00 C
 EST.\n\nOrganisation: Stimuleringsfonds Creatieve Industrie (Creative Indu
 stries Fund NL) in collaboration with Think Tanger\, Morocco\nLocation: Re
 sidency takes place at Think Tanger in Tangier\, Morocco. Applicants must 
 be established in the Netherlands\, Aruba\, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Saba\, Sin
 t Eustatius or Sint Maarten (Kingdom of the Netherlands) and registered in
  a business register within the Kingdom of the Netherlands.\nAward: EUR 5\
 ,500 subsidy for a two-month residency\, paid by the Creative Industries F
 und NL. No application fee.\nDuration: Two months in 2027\n\nMore: https:/
 /www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/open-call-residency-think-tanger?utm_s
 ource=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/open-call-residency-think-ta
 nger?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Residency takes place at Think Tanger in Tangier\, Morocco. Applic
 ants must be established in the Netherlands\, Aruba\, Bonaire\, Curacao\, 
 Saba\, Sint Eustatius or Sint Maarten (Kingdom of the Netherlands) and reg
 istered in a business register within the Kingdom of the Netherlands.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:playful-obscura-arthouse-games-residency-africa-2027@artificialnouveau.
 github.io
DTSTAMP:20261030T081527Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
SUMMARY:Deadline: Playful Obscura 2027: Arthouse Games Residency Africa (Ad
 dis Ababa\, Goethe-Institut and A MAZE.)
DESCRIPTION:Playful Obscura is the Goethe-Institut's arthouse games residen
 cy for Africa\, co-run with the Berlin playful-media festival A MAZE. Afte
 r editions in Ho (2025) and Accra (2026)\, the third edition moves to Addi
 s Ababa with Creative HUB Ethiopia\, the British Council and Alliance Ethi
 o-Francaise. WHAT IT IS: a three-week residency hosting two artists simult
 aneously to develop experimental\, artistic games and playful media\, with
  mentoring from the A MAZE. network and a public showcase. WHO: artists\, 
 game developers and creative technologists based in Africa who can work in
 dependently on a project\; the 2026 call drew 77 applications from 16 Afri
 can countries. WHAT YOU GET: travel and accommodation plus production supp
 ort\; the 2026 edition offered a production budget of up to EUR 1\,000 and
  a EUR 300 stipend\, and the 2027 figures should be confirmed in the full 
 call. APPLICATION: via the Goethe-Institut South Africa Playful Obscura pa
 ge. DEADLINE: 1 November 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Goethe-Institut Addis Abeb
 a\, with Creative HUB Ethiopia\, A MAZE.\, British Council and Alliance Et
 hio-Francaise\nLocation: Addis Ababa\, Ethiopia. For artists and game deve
 lopers based in Africa working in playful media and arthouse games.\nAward
 : Three-week funded residency hosting two artists at a time. 2027 financia
 l terms were not published in the call excerpt we could verify\; the 2026 
 Accra edition provided accommodation\, a production budget of up to EUR 1\
 ,000 and a EUR 300 stipend. No application fee.\nDuration: Residency 25 Ja
 nuary to 14 February 2027 in Addis Ababa\; open call 16 October to 1 Novem
 ber 2026\, with an online Q&A on 22 October.\n\nMore: https://www.goethe.d
 e/ins/za/en/kul/mut/p27.html?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
URL:https://www.goethe.de/ins/za/en/kul/mut/p27.html?utm_source=artificialn
 ouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Addis Ababa\, Ethiopia. For artists and game developers based in A
 frica working in playful media and arthouse games.
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
